c(62, "§7.1 era table (verbatim); §7.1 quarter table (verbatim); §7.1", "timeline", "Eras anchored on externally dated releases (E1 defined by the absence of release data) (verbatim): " + table("## 7.1 Method", 0) + " || quarterly series (verbatim): " + table("## 7.1 Method", 1) + " — E2 (the Badges block, 42 days) is the worst window on every measure: n=7, mean 2.14★, 57.1% money-negative, 71.4% rated 1–3★; 2025 Q4 is the lowest quarter (3.00★, 4 1★); 2026 Q3 has the highest money-negative count (5 of 9) at 4.44★.", "n/a", "mixed", "E1 36 / 4.50★ / 8.3% money-neg; E2 7 / 2.14★ / 57.1%; E3 28 / 4.61★ / 25.0%", "none", "table", "app-specific", ["13064284382", "14513739389"], "", "")

c(63, "§7.2", "timeline", "T1 the one-star episode of autumn 2025 — resolved, cause unknown: 6 1★ in 2025-08-26 → 2025-11-03; 0 before (32 reviews), 0 after (28 reviews, 10 months 3 days); inside mean 2.82★ / 54.5% 1–3★, outside 4.58★ / 11.7%; opens with a launch-crash regression 'the new update' that predates Apple's history, closes 7 days before v3.0; at n=7 in E2 'the 2.14★ mean is one or two reviews away from unremarkable' — treat the window as established and the explanation as open.", "n/a", "1★-burst", "6 1★ in 70 days; 0 in 10 months since", "none", "High-priority", "app-specific", ["13064284382", "13200826254", "13277885578", "13307114320", "13340807598", "13349206242"], "", "")

c(64, "§7.3; §8.5 #3", "timeline", "T2 monetization complaints changed register, not volume — persistent in volume, materially changed in character: 7 at 1.57★ pre-v3.0, 7 at 3.86★ since; the 2026 complaint is a retained user registering an objection — better for retention, worse for signal quality, 'the recent ratings no longer carry the monetization problem'; §8.5 do not read the 2026 rating recovery as the monetization problem resolving; confidence moderate (n=7 each half).", "n/a", "mixed", "1.57★ → 3.86★ across 14 money-negative reviews", "none", "moderate", "generalisable", ["14343374736", "14401503295", "14513739389"], "", "")

c(65, "§7.4", "timeline", "T3 defect reports fell to zero and stayed there — 5 defects between 2025-02-22 and 2025-08-26; the 37 reviews since contain none across 12 months and 3 major release blocks — the longest clean run of any theme; caveat: users who uninstall over a crash often do not return to review.", "fixed", "praise", "37 consecutive defect-free reviews", "none", "good (for this corpus)", "app-specific", ["13064284382"], "", "")

c(66, "§7.5", "timeline", "T4 the free-tier cap became visible in the second half — all 4 cap objections from 2025-11-03 onward: zero in the first 42 reviews, 4 in the last 29; three readings fit equally (cap tightened; always one habit and grew visible; chance at n=4) — no claim the cap changed; what is established is that all three who state a number state the same number.", "1-habit cap", "complaint", "0 of 42 → 4 of 29", "none", "weak", "app-specific", ["13349206242", "14080954809", "14209508686", "14355567891"], "", "")

c(67, "§7.6", "timeline", "T5 the developer-responsiveness signal stopped — all three PRAISE_DEV in the first 15% of the corpus by time (to 2025-04-09), none in the 61 reviews since; the shape is characteristic: early-adopter communities praise responsiveness, later cohorts do not notice it; cheap to check against actual response behaviour (no developer-reply field in the schema).", "n/a", "mixed", "3 of first 10; 0 of next 61", "do", "weak", "generalisable", ["12234759445", "12237444086", "12522499633"], "", "")

c(68, "§7.7", "insight", "What persisted across 603 days: the concept never drew a negative reaction — U:concept_positive in every one of 7 quarters, never below 4★; praise density 84.51% overall, by quarter 50% (2025 Q4) to 100% (2025 Q1, 2026 Q2), above 83% in six of seven; simplicity-as-emptiness never resolved (UX_TOO_MINIMAL 2025-02 → 2025-09, reappearing as UX_TRACKING_HARD 2026-07); nobody ever mentioned privacy, data loss, support, accessibility, battery, ads, a refund or a cancellation.", "n/a", "mixed", "concept-positive 7 of 7 quarters", "none", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["12893716000", "14359876847"], "", "")

c(69, "§7.8", "data-caveat", "What the corpus cannot say about time: nothing about the first 8.5 months in release terms (36 reviews predate Apple's history; v1 and v2 invisible); nothing about whether Badges or the Habit Forest worked — Badges mentioned by no reviewer at all, the Forest by exactly one (5★, as something bought, 8 months after v3.0) — two headline features, one mention; nothing about seasonality; nothing about release cadence vs sentiment (18 releases in 10 months from 2025-11-10, no reviewer reacting after 2025-04-09).", "n/a", "mixed", "Badges 0 mentions; Forest 1; 18 releases / 10 months", "none", "limited evidence", "generalisable", ["14331668442"], "", "two headline gamification releases went unremarked in reviews")

c(70, "Part 8 summary; §8.1.1; part 8 #1; §8.8 #1", "product-rule", "§8.1.1 state the free limit in the App Store description — one sentence ('The free version includes one habit; Premium unlocks unlimited habits') addresses the two lowest-rated complaints (cap_any 4 / 2.50★, MON_UNEXPECTED 2 / 1.50★; the description states no limit); 'the highest ratio of impact to effort available here' — it will not make anyone happier about the cap; it removes the surprise, which is what the 1★ and 2★ text objects to. One-line summary of the corpus: 'the product thesis is validated and the reliability is fine; everything that costs this app ratings happens at the free/paid boundary, and most of it is a disclosure and structure problem rather than a price problem.'", "undisclosed 1-habit cap", "complaint", "cap_any 4 / 2.50★; MON_UNEXPECTED 2 / 1.50★", "product-rule", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["13349206242", "14355567891", "13307114320"], "", "")

c(71, "§8.1.2; §8.1.3; §8.8 #2; part 8 #2", "must-have", "§8.1.2 show billing periods on every SKU and reduce the SKU count (10 SKUs, 3 names, no periods; 'a user who cannot tell what is being sold does not buy'); §8.1.3 settle the lifetime question in the description — if a lifetime SKU exists, say so: 'it is the only monetization attribute anyone in this corpus has ever praised by name'.", "10 SKUs, 3 names, no periods", "blocked-conversion", "3 conflicting lifetime beliefs; 1 2★ whose entire text is the question", "must-have", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["12552768633", "12652787691", "13941527190"], "", "")

c(72, "§8.1.4; part 8 #3", "do", "§8.1.4 name the features in the description — widgets, Apple Health, the calendar, badges and the Habit Forest are all absent from the description and present in reviews; two (widgets, Health) generated complaints from users who did not know what tier they were in.", "description omits six features", "complaint", "2 features produced complaints", "do", "external", "generalisable", ["13277885578", "12552768633"], "", "")

c(73, "§8.2.1; §8.8 #3; part 8 #4", "feature", "§8.2.1 'x times per week' scheduling — the only feature requested twice by users who otherwise rate 4★, 11 months apart; the use case is 'go to the gym three times a week, any three days'; a scheduling-model gap, not a nice-to-have, and it contradicts the product's own thesis: 'an app built on missing a day is fine still forces users to name the days'.", "absent", "complaint", "n=2, both 4★", "must-have", "Meaningful", "generalisable", ["12630919125", "13946139457"], "", "flexible frequency is thesis-consistent for a forgiving tracker")

c(74, "§8.2.2; part 8 #5", "feature", "§8.2.2 a multi-habit widget, and reconsider whether widgets belong behind the paywall — 'a widget is the cheapest daily-retention surface a habit tracker has, and this one is gated and limited to a single habit at the same time as the free tier is limited to a single habit'; 'I have to open the app to check which habits I have yet to complete'.", "per-habit widget, paid (n=1)", "complaint", "widget_gap 5 / 3.80★; paid-widget 1★", "build-free", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["13429536002", "13839542276", "13277885578", "12300467429"], "", "")

c(75, "§8.3.1; §8.3.2; §8.3.3; part 8 #6", "must-have", "§8.3 close the comprehension gap: explain the momentum number where it is displayed ('the gap between those two reviews is the whole opportunity' — one struggled then got it and became an advocate; a one-tap explanation converts a 3★ into a 5★ path); make the completion gesture unmissable (a 1★ in a habit app over the core action); give users a monthly hit-and-miss view (calendar_gap 3 — a calendar exists but is not doing this job; 'a filled month is the achievement feedback the streak used to provide').", "momentum unexplained; tick hard to find; calendar not showing hits/misses", "complaint", "comprehension 4 / 3.00★; UX_NO_TICK 1★; calendar_gap 3 / 3.33★", "must-have", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["12579762746", "12168189000", "13340807598", "12339835181", "12300467429"], "", "")

c(76, "§8.4.1; part 8 #7", "do", "§8.4.1 lead with the concept everywhere because it is the only thing with no detractors — the description and ASO title already do; the paywall does not: 'a user who converts is converting on the concept, and the concept is experienceable only with more than one habit'.", "concept not on the paywall", "praise", "concept 19 / 4.89★ / 0 below 4★", "do", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["12893716000", "13042199479"], "", "")

c(77, "§8.4.2; §8.6 table (verbatim)", "insight", "§8.4.2 reconsider the one-habit cap on strategy grounds, not review grounds — the report does not recommend raising it (no conversion data), but the decision should be made knowing that at one habit the product's own differentiator (forgiving multi-habit momentum) is not experienceable free, and that the reviewers who did convert converted on comparative value against trackers they had already tried — an informed judgement they could only make after using it. Experiments the corpus raises (verbatim): " + table("## 8.6 Experiments", 0), "1-habit cap", "mixed", "converters 3 (all COMP_TRIED_MANY / value); objectors 4", "research", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["13019604470", "12905347299", "13410412793", "13349206242"], "", "")

c(78, "§8.4.3; §8.4.4", "monetization", "§8.4.3 offer a trial or an unambiguous free window ('you can't really explore the app'; zero of 71 mention using a trial; the description mentions none) — the mechanism that would let the cap be tested without changing it; §8.4.4 fix the paywall prompt frequency (the 1★ titled 'annoying': the subscription 'keeps popping up' after the first habit).", "no trial; nagging prompt", "complaint", "MON_NO_TRIAL 1 / 4★; MON_PROMPT_NAG 1 / 1★", "research", "limited evidence", "generalisable", ["12530006457", "13349206242"], "", "")

c(79, "§8.5", "dont", "§8.5 do not: fund a reliability push ahead of disclosure (0 defects in 37 reviews / 12 months; the one open question is Apple Health); treat the 5★ share as satisfaction (17 of 50 five-star reviews, 34%, do not evidence satisfaction with anything); read the 2026 rating recovery as the monetization problem resolving (volume flat, complaints moved into 4–5★); build from the request backlog as a list (14 of 16 single-voice, one reviewer accounts for five); draw a country conclusion.", "n/a", "mixed", "17 of 50 5★ non-evidential; 14 of 16 requests single-voice", "dont", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["13604788620", "14401503295", "12234759445"], "", "")

c(80, "§8.7 #1, #2, #3, #4, #5, #6, #7", "insight", "§8.7 research questions: does a lifetime SKU currently exist (answerable in one minute in App Store Connect); what is the free-tier limit today and has it changed; what do the 268 silent raters think (0.27★ higher); why did the 1★ reviews stop on 2025-11-03; did Badges and the Habit Forest work (one mention between them); what happens after purchase (two of four payers had a bad experience, zero refund/cancellation mentions — the largest blank); why are Japan, Australia and Taiwan silent despite a shipped Japanese localisation.", "n/a", "mixed", "report gives none", "research", "limited evidence", "generalisable", ["12552768633", "12652787691", "14331668442"], "", "")

c(81, "§0.1 (thesis vs guilt)", "product-rule", "A forgiving score that decays instead of resetting is the whole value — 'missing a day does not reset / no guilt, punishment, anxiety or pressure' (CONCEPT_FORGIVING 11, 4.82★); 'I used to drop habits the second I missed a day — all because of streak pressure'; the streak is still shown alongside for those who want it.", "momentum decay + optional streak display", "praise", "CONCEPT_FORGIVING 11 / 15.49% / 4.82★", "product-rule", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["12893716000", "12753284542", "14237526621", "13634096636"], "", "")

